{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: model forecasts are generally above realized prices across most horizons; apply a small downward level shift (stronger beyond ~day 10).",
    "Overestimation of rallies/spikes: after upward moves in history, the model extrapolates too strongly; dampen forecast amplitudes (shrink deviations from the recent mean), especially for peaks.",
    "Insufficient mean reversion: true outcomes revert toward the recent range faster than the model; increase mean-reversion pull toward the last-30d average/median, particularly from day ~7 onward.",
    "Horizon-dependent drift: errors tend to grow with lead time (later days show larger overshoot); use a lead-time scaling where the correction magnitude increases with horizon.",
    "Turning-point lag: when the market rolls over, the model stays elevated for several days; introduce a regime check (if recent momentum weakens/turns negative, cap or step down the near-term path)."
  ]
}
